\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figures/fig-rq3-vmeasure.pdf}
\caption{RQ3: Leave-dataset-out mapping quality on 13{,}265 operations
from nine held-out datasets.
Dark bars show V-measure (cluster agreement between mapping-derived
\texttt{phase} and native \texttt{action} annotations);
light bars show boundary F1 (precision/recall of phase-transition
points). ``---'' marks datasets where boundary evaluation is
inapplicable. The dashed line marks 0.7.}
\Description{Grouped bar chart showing V-measure and boundary F1 for
nine held-out datasets, with a dashed threshold line at 0.7.}
\label{fig:rq3-vmeasure}
\end{figure}

Figure~\ref{fig:rq3-vmeasure} shows the results.
% Figure~\ref{fig:rq3-vmeasure} 展示了结果。
Seven of nine datasets exceed the 0.7 threshold on both V-measure and boundary F1, meaning the mapping rules trained on other datasets generalize: they assign operations to the correct semantic phase and detect phase transitions accurately.
% 9 个数据集中有 7 个在 V-measure 和边界 F1 上都超过 0.7 阈值，表明在其他数据集上训练的映射规则可泛化：它们将 operation 分配到正确的语义阶段并准确检测阶段转换。
The two low-scoring datasets (toolbench, api-bank) use atypical action vocabularies that the held-out mapping rules do not cover, confirming that the mapping is pattern-based and degrades gracefully when vocabulary shifts.
% 两个低分数据集（toolbench、api-bank）使用保留映射规则未覆盖的非典型操作词汇，确认映射是基于模式的，在词汇变化时优雅退化。

